usage: stability_driver.py [-h] --socket SOCKET --run-id RUN_ID --out-dir
                           OUT_DIR --events EVENTS --console-log CONSOLE_LOG
                           [--duration-seconds DURATION_SECONDS]
                           [--reload-count RELOAD_COUNT]
                           [--reload-interval-seconds RELOAD_INTERVAL_SECONDS]
                           [--reload-window-seconds RELOAD_WINDOW_SECONDS]
                           [--ready-timeout-seconds READY_TIMEOUT_SECONDS]
                           [--bootstrap-poll-seconds BOOTSTRAP_POLL_SECONDS]
                           [--poll-seconds POLL_SECONDS]
                           [--heartbeat-seconds HEARTBEAT_SECONDS]
                           [--profile PROFILE]
                           [--schedule-tolerance-seconds SCHEDULE_TOLERANCE_SECONDS]
                           [--connect-timeout-seconds CONNECT_TIMEOUT_SECONDS]

Run a 30-minute QMP-driven page reload stability sequence. The measured clock
starts only after the initial official page passes its strict PPM profile. Ten
real Ctrl+R key chords are scheduled two minutes apart; each reload must
produce a new strictly passing QEMU screendump. QEMU status is sampled every
30 seconds for the full hold. Guest process liveness is recorded separately by
autorun_mp_diag.sh and checked by stability_gate.py.

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --socket SOCKET
  --run-id RUN_ID
  --out-dir OUT_DIR
  --events EVENTS
  --console-log CONSOLE_LOG
                        live QEMU serial log written by t490_round.sh
  --duration-seconds DURATION_SECONDS
  --reload-count RELOAD_COUNT
  --reload-interval-seconds RELOAD_INTERVAL_SECONDS
  --reload-window-seconds RELOAD_WINDOW_SECONDS
  --ready-timeout-seconds READY_TIMEOUT_SECONDS
  --bootstrap-poll-seconds BOOTSTRAP_POLL_SECONDS
                        initial strict-page screendump interval; reloads use
                        --poll-seconds
  --poll-seconds POLL_SECONDS
  --heartbeat-seconds HEARTBEAT_SECONDS
  --profile PROFILE
  --schedule-tolerance-seconds SCHEDULE_TOLERANCE_SECONDS
  --connect-timeout-seconds CONNECT_TIMEOUT_SECONDS
